f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303275} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c2fef7-850a-5ab1-937e-404e56fd86a5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304657} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c37df1b-5ab5-50f0-a6f9-915619a890ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c37df1b-5ab5-50f0-a6f9-915619a890ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302538} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd4ece0a-4e3e-5490-96c4-f28e87a294cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b0aa435c-9e6e-5176-b913-9001e97b42f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-332588" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=3{x}_{1}(t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe systems of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n| ${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} |  |  | $\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-4}} |  | $\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |  | {{field-7}} |  |  | {{field-8}} |  |  |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+0\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=(-1)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eecbfc4-f7eb-5d4c-bea6-8fd21839804c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Form of a Particular Solution for Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89917edb-2315-5290-89a5-1760952c8a25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398762} {:answer/id #uuid "fffd262c-0068-596e-9ac0-00fd88b6bcf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398763} {:answer/id #uuid "3910513d-9f11-530f-a539-554e1501e899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398764} {:answer/id #uuid "fcdc809a-8332-5157-8c0a-6ec6b0d41dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398765} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd6675b-5072-5356-ae13-83e65ece4812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fffd262c-0068-596e-9ac0-00fd88b6bcf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398763} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9eb8731-2fb9-5537-93c3-a4e671793974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b74c0fe3-3f12-5992-93c1-45a8876eedf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-332739" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution has the same exponential factor, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eecbfc4-f7eb-5d4c-bea6-8fd21839804c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Form of a Particular Solution for Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a7977b-7339-57b7-a923-e8d0d8e4ad67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414500} {:answer/id #uuid "170117e4-3734-55f1-8a0e-dfa50d72211d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414501} {:answer/id #uuid "21d2e471-2f9a-5c9f-a4df-7096e53f0d75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414503} {:answer/id #uuid "2dcbc6a3-2212-5cc2-8998-578a7cd88408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414504} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a09ee3-dc65-57fb-bc76-d9010cfcc444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "170117e4-3734-55f1-8a0e-dfa50d72211d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414501} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a52ada-8c54-5615-81ca-fa8f0f0a0820" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414532}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47fd4ff4-6ba7-5ef0-9848-b6ea043ad002" :question/math-academy-id "q-332740" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+{e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere (\\mathbf{x}_c(t)) is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution has the same exponential factor, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305123 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eecbfc4-f7eb-5d4c-bea6-8fd21839804c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Form of a Particular Solution for Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0834d7b7-658d-5380-8dcb-fa6a807cb3d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-t}(t\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302511} {:answer/id #uuid "43ce2ff2-e4c9-5198-9e7f-3452f3b283ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302886} {:answer/id #uuid "c254ef35-09b4-54fc-a9c6-ef25dda4b6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303643} {:answer/id #uuid "c93347db-43ec-579b-9328-10764cc6c80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303691} {:answer/id #uuid "dc65b408-4dcd-5731-9fc0-0d1ad60e095a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c254ef35-09b4-54fc-a9c6-ef25dda4b6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303643} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4f527c6-9713-565d-b454-5da8600f2bba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "664eb982-2bc6-5ef7-b05c-2c605627127a" :question/math-academy-id "q-332805" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+2t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$ where ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+2t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is a polynomial in $t$ of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $2$, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={t}^{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166904 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dddc6159-ac4a-50ac-a366-08a4b809c925" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7057cef-7b3d-50a5-9d4e-de68d3e136cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7057cef-7b3d-50a5-9d4e-de68d3e136cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306723} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a56f792-0c53-5ead-9a98-fdc1db47d744" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307609} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28a19abb-54e8-5492-ad5c-9cc982d5b55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28a19abb-54e8-5492-ad5c-9cc982d5b55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305530} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b8e3c66-f507-5839-9243-fc157eef9444" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5cf6da1-456d-5dd5-897d-cda29a47d168" :question/math-academy-id "q-333007" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | $1$ |  | $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $0$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2}$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}(\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix})+\\begin{bmatrix}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} \\\\ -2{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{2} \\\\ -2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}0t+{a}_{1} \\\\ 0t+{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}({a}_{2}-2)t+({b}_{2}+1) \\\\ (-2{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+8)t+(-2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2})\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2}-2 &=0 \\\\ -2{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+8 &=0 \\\\ {b}_{2}+1 &={a}_{1} \\\\ -2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2} &={a}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving the first two equations, we get \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=2,\\,{a}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting these into the third and fourth equations, and solving for ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=0,\\,{b}_{1}=-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166904 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dddc6159-ac4a-50ac-a366-08a4b809c925" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0cfcb58-9d82-5239-b7a2-55b6a5aec3bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0cfcb58-9d82-5239-b7a2-55b6a5aec3bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414514} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f30c989-de06-575e-b0bb-9f683d4312c4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414524} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c89c95f-fe9b-52f0-91e5-40f76e3bbf32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c89c95f-fe9b-52f0-91e5-40f76e3bbf32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414507} :answer-field/id #uuid "72b4e588-1c2d-5b01-8c53-24f4c15496b7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414526} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3b0faf5-c52f-5e9a-a0b2-40242658a8f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3b0faf5-c52f-5e9a-a0b2-40242658a8f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414518} :answer-field/id #uuid "87ba22fc-b228-58c2-a360-feff99b2bf89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f0ab548-1239-59aa-8a8e-1144624f4ff6" :question/math-academy-id "q-333011" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}t+2 \\\\ t+1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | $1$ |  | $\\,\\,{t}^{2}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$ |  | $1$ |  | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $2$ |  |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2{a}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}2{a}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}(\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix})+\\begin{bmatrix}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2({a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1})-({a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}) \\\\ {a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}-3){t}^{2}+(2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}+4)t+(2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}-4) \\\\ ({a}_{1}-1){t}^{2}+({b}_{1}-2)t+({c}_{1}+1)\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}-3 &=0 \\\\ 2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}+4 &=2{a}_{1} \\\\ 2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}-4 &={b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1}-1 &=0 \\\\ {b}_{1}-2 &=2{a}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+1 &={b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving the fourth equation and then substituting the corresponding values ​​into the first and fifth equations to solve for ${a}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=1,\\,{a}_{2}=-1,\\,{b}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe substitute these into the second equation to solve for ${b}_{2},$ and then into the sixth and third equations to solve for ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ We finally get\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=2,\\,{c}_{1}=-1,\\,{c}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+1 \\\\ -\\,{t}^{2}+2t-2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308470 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166905 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d5ab3ac-770b-58c9-b30f-659773ea1a20" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1940783d-e9cc-57bd-8856-c5083ba67182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1940783d-e9cc-57bd-8856-c5083ba67182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305380} :answer-field/id #uuid "117c4376-c953-538e-9669-cbf9c4b80bd5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26832dff-38b0-5966-91ca-23fa74ae3537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26832dff-38b0-5966-91ca-23fa74ae3537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305512} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d6fc70c-1d60-5365-9ef6-117b3a1ce7d2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308017}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d664a12b-4a29-5994-b7c5-6826fe026444" :question/math-academy-id "q-333595" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{0} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3(0)}\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{-0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+1 \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1 &=3 \\\\ {c}_{2} &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=2.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=5.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+5\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166905 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d5ab3ac-770b-58c9-b30f-659773ea1a20" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "799b8f02-fb1f-5b98-b49f-34cc16e0e38d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "799b8f02-fb1f-5b98-b49f-34cc16e0e38d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306309} :answer-field/id #uuid "04152a47-43f0-5e2b-bd78-6166f9a81def" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29960f67-9b52-5584-afd6-b89d88082d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29960f67-9b52-5584-afd6-b89d88082d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305548} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef84e312-75bd-5b0f-abd8-1797baea8c93" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b979180-5d21-5395-8142-c8cb8588d387" :question/math-academy-id "q-333611" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}-{t}^{2}-2t+2 \\\\ -3{t}^{2}+5t-1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(0)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3(0)}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-(0)^{2}+2 \\\\ (0)^{2}-0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+2 \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2 &=8 \\\\ {c}_{2} &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=6.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=-7.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=6\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-7\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308480 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166905 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d5ab3ac-770b-58c9-b30f-659773ea1a20" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67fad082-3ca4-5f7b-a111-cbbb0ef6b4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67fad082-3ca4-5f7b-a111-cbbb0ef6b4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306141} :answer-field/id #uuid "2be14fd8-0c29-51cb-aa6e-12653917625e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307657} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de0056b8-ede6-586d-b252-9ce83cedf212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de0056b8-ede6-586d-b252-9ce83cedf212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307211} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9fc5883-695b-5830-8b8b-f8326bd7656f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f64f96f7-ae58-50bb-8fb6-64c4e2209bc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-333636" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0}\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+3 \\\\ -{c}_{2}+2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+3 &=7 \\\\ -{c}_{2}+2 &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=4.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=-5.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}-5\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166905 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d5ab3ac-770b-58c9-b30f-659773ea1a20" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "615faeab-4c34-5b69-a5b9-122defc6f4cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "615faeab-4c34-5b69-a5b9-122defc6f4cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306090} :answer-field/id #uuid "48905e48-2957-5752-8dae-6677e51d4a42" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "109a5a95-cf61-5472-8359-578a33ee94dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "109a5a95-cf61-5472-8359-578a33ee94dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305304} :answer-field/id #uuid "d378dc61-d74a-5e58-9b89-fef80e48a72e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a94fc120-f50c-5dd4-b643-1a93a1df3e1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-333638" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0)\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+1 \\\\ {c}_{2}-2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1 &=4 \\\\ {c}_{2}-2 &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=3.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=3.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}]}
